{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Check Permitted Development"},"description":"Purpose: prepare an England permitted-development evidence checklist, tentative class hint and restriction samples, without confirming a legal route. When to use: use for architect questions like \"is this rear extension PD?\", \"can I convert this Class E shop to flats?\", or \"does Article 4 affect this loft conversion\"; use check_planning_constraints when you only need raw constraints. Returns: pd_status always unclear, tentative candidate/applicable class, source states, sample flags, unknown counts and an authority-review checklist. All unresolved restriction evidence returns PD_EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE. Limitations: resolved England only; no legal applicability, current-law version, full-boundary intersection, dimensions, original building/use or permission-condition verification. Nearby records and null/small distances never prove containment or removal of a right. Source freshness/completeness are unverified; consult current legislation and the authority. The static keyword matcher is only a proposal hint. Parameter guidance: provide a full address/postcode and a concrete proposal phrase including use, works, and key dimensions where known. Chaining: every response returns site_ref; pass it unchanged into another Atlasly tool to reuse the canonical site, coordinates, boundary confidence, LPA, evidence links, and project context.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"address":{"description":"Site address or postcode for constraint-aware PD screening","minLength":3,"type":"string"},"proposal":{"description":"Proposal text, e.g. \"single-storey rear extension under 4m\", \"loft conversion with dormer\", or \"Class E shop to C3 flats\"","minLength":4,"type":"string"},"site_ref":{"description":"Canonical site_ref returned by any previous Atlasly tool. Pass it unc